/-!
# Regular polynomial formal fibres over a regular local base in characteristic zero

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, proof of Proposition 07PV, paragraphs 3--4,
with the hypersurface derivation argument of Lemma 07PU.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-regular-base-formal-fibre)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

namespace Polynomial

/-- The formal fibre above zero over a characteristic-zero regular local base is regular.
Source: Stacks Project, proof of Proposition 07PV, paragraphs 3--4, and the second
paragraph of the proof of Lemma 07PU.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-regular-base-formal-fibre)

Proof:
The localization of A[X] at q is regular local (Mathlib's polynomial localization
regularity theorem), and its completion C is regular local by 07NY, hence regular
by 0AFS. If r = 0, its fibre is a localization of C and is regular.
Otherwise let K be the fraction field of A. The extension of r to K[X] is a nonzero
prime, hence generated by an irreducible f. Invert the nonzero elements of A in C
to obtain the regular ring R. Localization and quotient identify the fibre with R/(f):
the residue field at r is the field K[X]/(f). Extend d/dX from A[X] to its localization,
completion and then R by 07PE; it kills K and sends f to f'. Since K has characteristic
zero, f and f' are coprime. Their Bezout identity shows that the image of D(f) is a unit
in R/(f). The hypersurface derivation criterion 07PF gives regularity of R/(f), and
transport along the fibre isomorphism concludes. No completeness assumption on A is
needed: regularity of its polynomial localization and completion suffices. -/
theorem regularBase_formalFibre_isRegular
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A] [CharZero A]
    (q : Ideal (Polynomial A)) [q.IsMaximal]
    (hq : q.comap (Polynomial.C : A →+* Polynomial A) = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    (r : Ideal (Polynomial A)) [r.IsPrime] (hrq : r ≤ q)
    (hrA : r.comap (Polynomial.C : A →+* Polynomial A) = ⊥) :
    IsRegularRing (r.Fiber
      (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q))
        (Localization.AtPrime q))) := by sorry

end Polynomial
